# Flutter Design Protocol

Overrides the "Hard rules" in `DESIGN_FIX_PROMPT.md` and `DESIGN_SPEC.md` where they conflict.

## Aesthetic
- No boxy Material templates or stock Cards. Prefer asymmetric grids, staggered offsets, expanding sheet headers and contextual depth.
- Surfaces: semantic gradients, subtle `BackdropFilter` blur, 1px micro-borders at 0.05–0.1 opacity. Dark mode uses rich charcoal/deep slate, not pure black.
- Typography is structure: mix `FontWeight.w300` with `w800`, use size scale and `letterSpacing` instead of heavy containers.
- Every tappable widget gives physical feedback (`AnimatedScale` press, `AnimatedContainer`, custom `Curves`). No instant layout jumps.
- Stats/data: minimal abstract geometry (`CustomPainter`) over stock chart libraries unless told otherwise. Subtle accent dots/lines are welcome.

## Engineering
- No unused imports; delete dead files during structural changes.
- `const` wherever possible; no overflows (Flexible/Expanded, `maxLines` + `overflow`).
- Keep widget files small: extract private sub-widgets instead of 500-line trees.
- Add needed packages (`google_fonts`, `flutter_animate`, ...) to `pubspec.yaml` and resolve them.
- Fix compiler errors and lifecycle bugs before reporting done.

## Guardrails (production app)
- Presentation layer only: do not change Firestore queries, providers' logic, models, repositories or RBAC checks.
- Keep `lib/core/a11y/semantics_ext.dart` semantics and 48px tap targets; respect `MediaQuery.disableAnimations`.
- Colours and tokens live in `lib/core/theme/`; screens read them from the theme, not hard-coded.
